# /etc/biokids is shipped so that dpkg owns it and removes it on purge once the
# secrets the postinst generated are gone.
#
# /var/lib/biokids, /var/log/biokids and /run/biokids are deliberately NOT here:
# dpkg re-applies the recorded mode of a directory it ships on every unpack, and
# 0700 on a family's history must not depend on nobody having changed the
# recorded mode. The postinst creates those three instead.
etc/biokids
usr/share/biokids
